        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vance%2C_Alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1879, the town was renamed Vance after physician William Vance, who founded the Lee Institute school.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vance%2C_Alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Alabama Great Southern Railroad arrived in 1873, ending stagecoach mail delivery and linking Vance to regional trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/vance/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Vance formally incorporated in 1972, solidifying its municipal status after more than a century of growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
